\description{
\code{plan_psock_min()} sizes a cluster from \code{\link[parallelly:freeCores]{parallelly::freeCores()}}, which reads
a \emph{trailing} load average (5 minutes by default). Two clusters built inside
that window therefore both observe the same idle cores and both claim them:
the load produced by the first has not yet reached the average the second
reads. Staggering the builds by more than the averaging window papers over
this; it does not fix it, and it forces callers to hand-tune both the stagger
and the number of concurrent jobs against the size of the fleet.

These functions keep a small ledger of what has actually been handed out, so
allocation is based on \emph{reservations} rather than on a lagging measurement.
Each successful build records \code{host -> workers} (and the memory those workers are expected to need,
\code{memGB}) under a reservation id owned by the building process; \code{\link[=freeCoresLessReserved]{freeCoresLessReserved()}} subtracts those from the
measured free cores. Releases are keyed by id, because one process may hold
several clusters at once.

The ledger is self-healing: every read drops entries whose owning process is
no longer alive, so a master that is killed without releasing cannot leak a
reservation forever. A process id means something only on the machine it ran on, so each reservation id
starts with that machine's nodename (\verb{<nodename>:<random>}; the columns of the ledger are unchanged, as
older versions of this package share the file) and only rows owned by the reading machine, or by none
(an id without a nodename), are checked; a row owned by another machine is left to that machine.
A host named \code{"localhost"} or \code{"127.0.0.1"} in a row is the owner's machine, not the reader's.
}
\section{Scope}{

The ledger is a file, so it is shared by every process that can see that file
-- which is what is needed when several worker panes on one machine each build
their own cluster over a shared fleet. If \emph{different} machines build clusters
over the same fleet, point them all at one path on shared storage via
\code{options(clusters.reservationsPath = )}. Machines that share a home folder (a Slurm cluster) share the
default path, and so the ledger, without doing anything.
